cut buffer size.&nbsp; The solution is to use KED under RT-11 with<br>
a Mapped Monitor as a Virtual Job.&nbsp; Fortunately, DEC did<br>
provide a simple way to do that (although under certain conditions,<br>
there can be a serious problem).&nbsp; The solution is to use VBGEXE<br>
to run KED.SAV in which case the cut buffer seem to be about<br>
10 K bytes as opposed to only about 2 K bytes when KEX.SAV<br>
is used.<br>
<br>
Jerome Fine<br>
